% Regression guard for checkbar() in genmidi.c, which builds the warning
% "Track %d Bar %d has %d/%d time units while the time signature has %d in
% repeat" for a bar of the wrong length.  The message used to be built in an
% 80-byte buffer, too small once the bar length is a fraction with large
% terms.  The -BF 2 stress model produces such fractions (e.g. 4499/500), but
% this sample gets there without it, so that the guard does not depend on
% the stress model: the incomplete tuplets (only 2, 3, 3 and 3 of their 3,
% 5, 7 and 11 notes) make the last bar, bar 10 counting from 0, 19207/1155
% units long, and its warning on the second time through the repeat takes
% 82 characters.
% Under the sanitize build the overflow aborts abc2midi, failing this test.
X:1
T:Bar check warning longer than 80 characters
C:abc2midi test
M:12/8
L:1/8
K:D
FAA dAA BAB dAG|FAA dfe dBA BAG|FAA dAA BAB dAG|FAA dfe dBA d3|
|:dfe dfa gfe fdB|AFA dfe dBA BAG|dfe dfa gfe fdB|AFA dfe dBA d3|
dfe dfa gfe fdB|AFA dfe dBA BAG|
(3:2:2AB (5:4:3cde (7:4:3fga (11:8:3ABc d3 A3 A3:|
